On Wed, 29 Oct 2003, Haakon Studebaker wrote:
> Is there a way where Nethack starts that if one enters a name then that
> character archetype will be rolled up and ready to play? Say I want to play
> a monk, I'll use "heptapod" or if I wanted to play a samurai I'll use
> "Kuresu" which would cut down on the time consuming chore of typing nmmc
> and so forth.

You can create a batch file that launches NetHack with different options
based on the name you enter. Here's an example. Cut and paste the
following 8 lines into Notepad, and save it as nh.bat in your NetHack
folder (make sure Notepad doesn't name rename it to nh.bat.txt).

======cut here==========
@echo off

set role=
if "%1"=="heptapod" set role=-monk-male-chaotic
if "%1"=="Kuresu" set role=-samurai-male
if "%1"=="Sally" set role=-wizard-human-female-chaotic

nethack -u%1%role%
======cut here============

Now, when you want to play NetHack, instead of typing
   C:\Program Files\NetHack
type this instead:
   C:\Program Files\nh Kuresu

